# Satellite repos — push rules for agents

The `aicom` folder is a **dev monorepo**. Several subfolders have **their own GitHub repos** and must **NOT** be pushed to `alexar76/aicom` via plain `git push`.

## Source of truth

- Map: `scripts/satellite-map.yaml`
- Orchestrator: `scripts/publish_all_repos.sh` (idempotent)
- Single satellite: `scripts/publish_satellite.sh <id>` or `scripts/mirror_satellites.sh --satellite <id>`
- Factory only: `scripts/publish_aicom_factory.sh`

## When user asks to "push" or "publish"

| Intent | Command |
|--------|---------|
| Everything (satellites + trimmed aicom) | `./scripts/publish_all_repos.sh` |
| All satellites only | `./scripts/publish_all_repos.sh --satellites-only` |
| Trimmed aicom factory only | `./scripts/publish_all_repos.sh --factory-only` |
| One repo | `./scripts/publish_all_repos.sh --satellite <id>` |

Set `GH_PAT` or `GITHUB_TOKEN` for authenticated pushes.

**Do NOT** run `git push origin main` on the monorepo root to update public GitHub — that uploads satellite folders into `aicom`.

